00:08:09.743 --> 00:08:11.784
or the book is naturally good

00:08:11.784 --> 00:08:14.063
and gets recommended from somebody else,

00:08:14.063 --> 00:08:16.265
and it finds its way to that person.

00:08:16.265 --> 00:08:19.338
But, you know, approaching something with,

00:08:19.338 --> 00:08:21.502
"Hey, everybody, you know, like,

00:08:21.502 --> 00:08:24.755
I've seen this work 'cause
my speaking career is epic,

00:08:24.755 --> 00:08:26.311
and people fucking love it,"

00:08:26.311 --> 00:08:28.894
that comes across as tone deaf.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:33.691
So, it's fucking a million other people.

00:08:33.691 --> 00:08:35.593
- Yeah, yeah, it's just,

00:08:35.593 --> 00:08:38.600
it's so much work to put into one product,

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:42.061
it launches, it's doing really
good in that period of time,

00:08:42.061 --> 00:08:43.815
and then you feel like, that's it,

00:08:43.815 --> 00:08:47.868
should I continue pushing
or should I allow time?

00:08:47.868 --> 00:08:50.142
- You should definitely keep pushing.

00:08:50.142 --> 00:08:52.001
You should always push,

00:08:52.001 --> 00:08:53.862
if you want it to be successful.

00:08:53.862 --> 00:08:56.075
Like, it's gonna breed without you,

00:08:56.075 --> 00:08:57.312
even while you're pushing.

00:08:57.312 --> 00:08:59.038
Those things are happening in parallel,

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:02.227
they're not individually situations.

00:09:02.227 --> 00:09:03.212
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:09:03.212 --> 00:09:05.541
It just feels a little bit
like postpartum depression,

00:09:05.541 --> 00:09:07.790
you know, when you push
the baby out and then.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.120
- Well, because you know that,

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.674
obviously, that's a different
scenario altogether but

00:09:12.674 --> 00:09:17.435
what I see with a lot of
authors is their expectations.

00:09:17.435 --> 00:09:19.502
People create this narrative in their mind

00:09:19.502 --> 00:09:21.137
that this book is gonna come out,

00:09:21.137 --> 00:09:23.258
and it's going to become a viral sensation

00:09:23.258 --> 00:09:24.541
and they're gonna be on "Today's Show"

00:09:24.541 --> 00:09:27.959
and every influencer is gonna
be posting a copy of it,

00:09:27.959 --> 00:09:29.544
and their fame is gonna explode

00:09:29.544 --> 00:09:32.203
and they're gonna start
making 10 times more speaking,

00:09:32.203 --> 00:09:34.257
and they create all these scenarios

00:09:34.257 --> 00:09:36.432
without realizing the
world's got a million things

00:09:36.432 --> 00:09:39.503
to look at besides their book.

00:09:39.503 --> 00:09:41.613
- Yeah, I think that's the hardest part,

00:09:41.613 --> 00:09:45.788
like the expectations, right,
of what we put into it.

00:09:45.788 --> 00:09:46.621
- I think so too.

00:09:46.621 --> 00:09:49.454
I think that, listen, it requires,

00:09:50.784 --> 00:09:52.772
micro speed and macro patience.

00:09:52.772 --> 00:09:53.771
On a day to day basis,

00:09:53.771 --> 00:09:58.271
you have to keep pushing,
pushing, pushing on.

00:09:58.271 --> 00:10:00.252
In the real game, I still get to,

00:10:00.252 --> 00:10:01.896
People tweet me, this weekend

00:10:01.896 --> 00:10:04.038
